        "name": "MLB SlugFest 2004",
        "summary": "The second title in Midway's baseball series, SlugFest 20-04 continues to pour on the rough-housing gameplay, bizarre codes, and humorous commentary. In addition to the new Home Run Derby mode and Create-A-Team options, the game features the ability of pitchers to catch \"On Fire\" and impossible Special Pitches that zigzag, arc, and whizz by in ways that would leave any batter humiliated. New secret teams have been added to the previous bunch, including aliens, minotaurs, and Sub-Zero of Mortal Kombat fame. The customizable Instant Replay is another nice touch, allowing you to relive the awkward moments once you pause the game. And, of course, Tim Kitzrow and Jim Shorts return to the commentators' booth, making their signature random comments and incessant arguments.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7l5c.jpg",
        "release_date": 1047859200,
        "rating": 36.0,
        "rating_count": 1,
        "genres": "Sport",
        "platform_ids": "11,21,24,8",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/mlb-slugfest-2004",
        "cached_at": 1772527922
      },
      {
        "id": 24065,
        "name": "Naruto: Ninja Council 2",
        "summary": "Action game, based on the Shonen Jump manga. This sequel to the very first Naruto game on the GBA (the second game was a much different simulation/adventure) has three-times the amount of stages and characters twice the size. The action is streamlined and more dynamic. Players can transform into Naruto, Sasuke and Sakura and use their abilities to defeat the scrolling stages. The game also utilizes the link cable for a two-player co-op mode and for a four-player battle mode.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1uba.jpg",
