      },
      {
        "id": 166322,
        "name": "Harry Potter and the Chamber of Secrets",
        "summary": "Harry Potter and the Chamber of Secrets is the second game in the series for the Game Boy Advance. Like its predecessor, it is an action adventure game but this time with an isometric perspective. In Harry's second year at Hogwarts, the ancient Chamber of Secrets has been opened, and what lurks within is attacking students. To get through this ordeal alive, Harry must again complete various challenges. These mostly consist of navigating large mazes, fighting monsters, solving puzzles, flipping switches and pressing buttons for doors to open. As Harry is often in places he shouldn't be, stealth sequences are also a large part of the game. To avoid teachers and prefects, he can sneak around slowly and hide behind curtains. If he is caught, he is thrown out and house points can be deducted. Finally, Quidditch is also back in this game, this time in three-dimensional space, viewed from the back.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3rbi.jpg",
        "release_date": 1037318400,
        "rating": 55.08554808076624,
        "rating_count": 8,
        "genres": null,
        "platform_ids": "24",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/harry-potter-and-the-chamber-of-secrets--2",
        "cached_at": 1772527922
      },
      {
        "id": 166333,
        "name": "Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire",
        "summary": "Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire for the Nintendo DS and Game Boy Advance is a top-down action/adventure game where you play as the three friends and progress through the story based on the book and film. Make your way through various scenarios by attacking enemies and solving puzzles using spells. One button fires a ranged spell, such as Confoundus, while another is used for stream spells, like Wingardium Leviosa, which can be moved around with the Control Pad. You can also call your friends for added power to your magical spells. The DS version includes a small bonus game where you take care of a magical creature called a 'Niffler'. It is a simulation game, like a very simple Tamagotchi. You can feed the Niffler, clean it, and give it toys. Depending on what you do, it will become more or less pleased with you. Perform well enough, and it will become really happy, and let you pat it to make it even happier.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3rbv.jpg",
        "release_date": 1131408000,
        "rating": 70.02576940936915,
        "rating_count": 7,
        "genres": "Adventure",
        "platform_ids": "24",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/harry-potter-and-the-goblet-of-fire--1",
        "cached_at": 1772527922
      },
      {
        "id": 166336,
        "name": "Harry Potter and the Order of the Phoenix",
        "summary": "In both the Nintendo DS and GBA versions, the player can walk around Hogwarts in almost 3D pre-rendered backgrounds, like in the first Resident Evil games. The gameplay consists in various minigames, which you play either by pressing buttons on the right timing or by doing different kinds of moves with your stylus on the touch-screen.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3rc0.jpg",
        "release_date": 1182729600,
